on loan.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian birth tourism to Brazil increases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a279f3746e0e03a53baafa690b27dcf8240655d79239963ab2c573a6b5909073</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T19:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-birth-tourism-to-brazil-increases/a-79312304--01a0fcbb92e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-birth-tourism-to-brazil-increases/a-79312304?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine and stricter regulations in Argentina, more and more Russians are choosing to travel to Brazil to give birth to children, who will obtain Brazilian nationality.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A war-fatigued and anxious Russia picks a new parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ecce66e2ae4d6331f746c8912c28dbf05ebe400b5bc5b145aadec34853cb4f5</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-war-fatigued-and-anxious-russia-picks-a-new-parliament/a-79312440--1588122e0cc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-war-fatigued-and-anxious-russia-picks-a-new-parliament/a-79312440?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fuel shortages, drone strikes and mobilization rumors are fueling anxiety and war fatigue in Russia. As support for peace talks grows among Russians, the Kremlin is watching closely ahead of parliamentary elections.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Smuggling suspected as more rare animals seen in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f7904d7edc46966f02cb02afc62656b7fe4676ea30e8012c66e1025d4eb0c5b</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/smuggling-suspected-as-more-rare-animals-seen-in-india/a-79309352--d0621e7dbde3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/smuggling-suspected-as-more-rare-animals-seen-in-india/a-79309352?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Orangutans, rare reptiles and other exotic animals are popping up in India, suggesting the country is becoming a major destination for trafficked wildlife.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: How disinformation fuels Houthi-Saudi conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c7146a1d7e12718e9993bd6c2b3e614ff34c198394f5d9b306479e0a538117c</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T12:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-how-disinformation-fuels-houthi-saudi-conflict/a-79307257--b5d0251bde9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-how-disinformation-fuels-houthi-saudi-conflict/a-79307257?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As fighting between the Houthis and Saudi Arabia escalates, old and repurposed videos have flooded social media, with many presented as fresh footage from the front lines.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian President Vucic criticizes Kosovo war crimes verdict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f6eaf3a4fd04cdbdef9d3bc8405c8636d360d14bb4a7511085d6f68309cbacd</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-s-president-vucic-criticizes-kosovo-war-crimes-verdict/a-79307654--c1957e85b089.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbian-president-vucic-criticizes-kosovo-war-crimes-verdict/a-79307654?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The conviction of four former Kosovo Liberation Army leaders has drawn sharply different reactions across the Balkans. Serbia has accused the court of failing to fully address crimes against Serbs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>King Charles, Earl Spencer clash over Diana death once again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bfb338427b66c6480869be4556e0b93aec98fa7302eab6773ecccad99a77ab1</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/king-charles-earl-spencer-clash-over-diana-death-once-again/a-79305876--fe22dce63256.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/king-charles-earl-spencer-clash-over-diana-death-once-again/a-79305876?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Buckingham Palace has rejected criticism of King Charles III in a new book by the brother of his late wife, Princess Diana. Earl Charles Spencer has been a fierce critic of his former brother-in-law for decades.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK: Village votes to 'secede' in asylum center plan protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86e4f46ff7d0c36814d8ae5f1216f8ec5463619ff5c890bac9e7a7d9639a8459</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T17:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-village-votes-to-secede-in-asylum-center-plan-protest/a-79295826--f45e2135fb80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-village-votes-to-secede-in-asylum-center-plan-protest/a-79295826?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Residents of Piddington, a tiny, remote village in Oxfordshire in England, have staged a "referendum" on leaving the UK. They are objecting to plans to open an asylum reception center at a disused military base nearby.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Canada and the EU deepen ties to counter Trump?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4aa52900378a58302bdc1b15d4cf778c63fc28ff4d8fee09070a0aea56d35dbc</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-canada-and-the-eu-deepen-ties-to-counter-trump/a-79295388--7ecef7e34741.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-canada-and-the-eu-deepen-ties-to-counter-trump/a-79295388?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney is known for standing up to US President Donald Trump. Now he wants to forge a "unique alliance" with Europe. But what could such a partnership look like?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Shock in Kosovo as Hague convicts former President Thaci</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8d1a53f4f64bc897608fb6068fef971aea09250beef76e07b980e5187f13864</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T15:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/shock-in-kosovo-as-hague-convicts-former-president-thaci/a-79294916--a5436d550055.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/shock-in-kosovo-as-hague-convicts-former-president-thaci/a-79294916?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The conviction in The Hague of former President Hashim Thaci and three former Kosovo Liberation Army leaders has caused consternation in Kosovo — both among political leaders and on the streets. DW reports from Pristina.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>British-American writer Bonnie Greer dies aged 77</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed561930f359e3393680b095c9b9310bfc1109c78d1b0515353051abe5ca056d</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/british-american-writer-bonnie-greer-dies-aged-77/a-79293174--ca7cae1c3055.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/british-american-writer-bonnie-greer-dies-aged-77/a-79293174?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chicago-born playwright Bonnie Greer, who became a familiar face in British political discourse later in life, has died. Her husband David Hutchins announced news of Greer's death.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How the Houthis are also putting Egypt under pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce203b7e1b1aff8c371820aa9f455c246e81f5ae16faf8d467559a2288ca4bb9</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T13:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-the-houthis-are-also-putting-egypt-under-pressure/a-79291103--b1d138b096dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-the-houthis-are-also-putting-egypt-under-pressure/a-79291103?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Houthis, a Yemeni rebel group, are expanding their control of maritime corridors in the Red Sea area. Their target is their avowed enemy Saudi Arabia. But the military moves also endanger Egypt.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
